00:07:44.480 --> 00:07:49.320
answer any questions that nobody's

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:51.080
asking us. It is that easy. Because why

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:53.280
are we volunteering information about

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.360
ourselves constantly? If someone asks us

00:07:53.280 --> 00:07:57.520
how was our weekend, we launch into a

00:07:55.360 --> 00:07:59.480
15-minute monologue about every detail.

00:07:57.520 --> 00:08:01.520
Or if someone asks what we do for work,

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:03.280
and we explain our entire resume or our

00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:05.880
side projects. So let's try this

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:07.960
instead. If someone asks you a question,

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:10.240
answer what they ask and nothing more

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:11.640
and just let that sit. So for example,

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:14.080
"How was your weekend?" "It was really

00:08:11.640 --> 00:08:16.240
good actually. I really needed some good

00:08:14.080 --> 00:08:18.120
old rest and relaxation." And just stop

00:08:16.240 --> 00:08:20.120
there and smile at them. If they're

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.720
curious, let them follow up if they want

00:08:20.120 --> 00:08:23.919
to. That's how you get people to be more

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:25.560
intrigued in you. So it's not about

00:08:23.919 --> 00:08:27.600
being cold or stand-offish or

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:30.040
withholding yourself too much. You can

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:32.159
still be all of that and be selective

00:08:30.040 --> 00:08:33.800
about what you choose to reveal. In

00:08:32.159 --> 00:08:35.919
fact, all of these things together like

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:38.320
warmth plus your discernment and

00:08:35.919 --> 00:08:40.039
selectiveness is so powerful. Think

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:41.919
about it like this. Imagine two types of

00:08:40.039 --> 00:08:43.680
