00:08:41.919 --> 00:08:46.000
is very friendly. She shares a lot,

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.200
talks a lot over everything, and she

00:08:46.000 --> 00:08:50.080
overshares a bit but is very likable.

00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:52.960
But then you kind of don't remember her.

00:08:50.080 --> 00:08:55.200
But person B is equally friendly and

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:56.600
warm, asks some really great questions,

00:08:55.200 --> 00:08:58.640
and laughs at people's jokes, makes

00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.960
people feel seen. But when you leave the

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:01.640
dinner, you realize that you don't even

00:08:59.960 --> 00:09:03.280
know anything about person B. And that's

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:04.760
why you can't stop thinking about them.

00:09:03.280 --> 00:09:06.520
Someone who is comfortable not being the

00:09:04.760 --> 00:09:08.760
center of every single conversation is

00:09:06.520 --> 00:09:10.280
also very comfortable with the idea that

00:09:08.760 --> 00:09:11.600
not everyone deserves to know

00:09:10.280 --> 00:09:13.440
everything. And then you also get to

00:09:11.600 --> 00:09:14.720
