like, "I work with an international

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:34.800
company." Which is still kind of vague.

00:09:33.320 --> 00:09:37.000
And now their brain is starting to fill

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:38.560
in some blanks like, "What do you do?

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:39.880
Like what are you selling? They still

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:41.960
don't know anything. And because they

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:43.440
don't know, they want to learn more and

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:45.680
they're curious. So, people will

00:09:43.440 --> 00:09:47.160
continue to ask follow-up questions. Do

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:48.320
you see what I'm saying? They become

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:49.920
more and more interested in you. It's

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:51.800
not like you're lying or anything. You

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:53.360
just answer the questions. And here's an

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:55.280
even more powerful move. Redirect the

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:56.720
attention, like, "Oh, what about you?

00:09:55.280 --> 00:09:58.160
What do you do?" Because here's the

00:09:56.720 --> 00:10:00.840
thing about human nature and not enough

00:09:58.160 --> 00:10:02.480
people understand this concept. Everyone

00:10:00.840 --> 00:10:04.400
wants to talk about themselves, every

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:07.040
single one of us. So, when someone gives

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:09.920
us room to actually do that and listen

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:12.560
to us, we walk away thinking, "Wow, that

00:10:09.920 --> 00:10:14.440
person is amazing." Because they made us

00:10:12.560 --> 00:10:16.320
feel seen. And there are studies that

00:10:14.440 --> 00:10:18.080
have shown people rate others as better

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:20.440
communicators and more relatable and

00:10:18.080 --> 00:10:22.960
more charming, the more they listen and

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:24.840
ask questions and not the opposite. The

00:10:22.960 --> 00:10:27.360
best conversationalists are always the

00:10:24.840 --> 00:10:29.360
best listeners. So, try this. Don't

00:10:27.360 --> 00:10:31.320
bother with information about your life

00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:33.600
unless someone asks you. Don't dump your

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:35.920
feelings or your opinions unless there's

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:37.800
a good reason to. Instead, focus on

00:10:35.920 --> 00:10:39.720
staying present in conversation, being

00:10:37.800 --> 00:10:41.360
curious, asking great questions. Make

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:42.720
the person or the people in front of you

00:10:41.360 --> 00:10:44.320
feel like they're the most interesting

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:46.040
people in the room. So, when they think

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:47.720
about you later, they're actually more

00:10:46.040 --> 00:10:49.600
curious because they realize, "Wow, I

00:10:47.720 --> 00:10:50.920
just had this most amazing conversation

00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:53.200
with this person and I don't know

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.600
anything about them." So, focus on being

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:57.320
interested and make the person you're

00:10:54.600 --> 00:10:58.520
talking to feel special and find things

00:10:57.320 --> 00:11:00.720
about other people that you find

00:10:58.520 --> 00:11:03.000
intriguing and ask them to tell you

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:05.400
more. That's the whole secret to being

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:06.920
magnetic because imagine your inner

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:09.200
world as a house of a lot of rooms,

00:11:06.920 --> 00:11:10.480
right? The moment someone walks in, most

00:11:09.200 --> 00:11:12.040
people will probably open every single

00:11:10.480 --> 00:11:13.800
door and be like, "Here's my childhood

00:11:12.040 --> 00:11:15.520
trauma room. Here's my insecurity room.

00:11:13.800 --> 00:11:16.880
And here's my hallway of failed

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:19.280
relationships." But the person with a

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.160
lot of mystique will open the front door

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.720
warmly, let them into the living room,

00:11:21.160 --> 00:11:24.280
make them tea, and make them feel

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:26.040
welcome. But then all of these other

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:27.680
rooms are behind closed doors and

00:11:26.040 --> 00:11:29.839
they're not being offered to you unless

00:11:27.680 --> 00:11:31.320
you have earned the invitation. Another

00:11:29.839 --> 00:11:33.240
concept is what I call the phantom

00:11:31.320 --> 00:11:35.000
principle and I cringe whenever someone

00:11:33.240 --> 00:11:36.120
says, "Oh, it's easy for you to say all

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:37.840
of this because you're pretty." Like,

00:11:36.120 --> 00:11:39.560
girl, yes, I know, but there are also

00:11:37.840 --> 00:11:40.760
plenty of pretty people in the world who

00:11:39.560 --> 00:11:43.520
don't know how to use that to their

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:45.400
advantage. Presence over beauty every

00:11:43.520 --> 00:11:47.040
single time. You have to learn to create

00:11:45.400 --> 00:11:48.760
a signature for yourself. Think about

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:51.160
The Phantom of the Opera, for example.

00:11:48.760 --> 00:11:54.120
He's one of the most iconic romantic

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:56.480
figures in literature, and by design, he

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:58.520
is actually disfigured. Because of that,

00:11:56.480 --> 00:12:00.840
he wears a mask, he hides in the

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:02.400
shadows, and yet his romantic interest

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:04.840
and everyone who has ever read or seen

00:12:02.400 --> 00:12:07.880
that story is so drawn to him with such

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:09.800
intensity. Why? Because the phantom

00:12:07.880 --> 00:12:11.280
understood that mystique is not about

00:12:09.800 --> 00:12:13.040
how you look, but about how you make

00:12:11.280 --> 00:12:14.920
people feel when you're present with

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.400
them. Also, how you make them feel when

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:18.160
you're not present. But here's the

00:12:16.400 --> 00:12:20.120
nuance, and this is important. You

00:12:18.160 --> 00:12:21.640
cannot be mysterious without being

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:24.000
interesting or having some form of

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:26.680
substance. The phantom was a musical

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:28.160
genius. His aesthetic is also iconic.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:29.720
And even thinking about, for example,

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.000
Beyoncé, I don't know a single quote

00:12:29.720 --> 00:12:33.360
from her, but she has amazing visuals,

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:35.480
and she's one of the biggest pop stars

00:12:33.360 --> 00:12:37.520
in the world. The mystery only works

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:39.160
because there's substance behind it. So,

00:12:37.520 --> 00:12:40.720
let's also talk about the signature real

00:12:39.160 --> 00:12:42.320
quick. A signature is something that's

00:12:40.720 --> 00:12:44.880
so distinct and different from other

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:46.640
people and belongs to them so much so

00:12:44.880 --> 00:12:48.200
that it becomes inseparable from who

00:12:46.640 --> 00:12:50.200
they are. Now, this doesn't even have to

00:12:48.200 --> 00:12:52.040
be incredibly impressive as long as it's

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:53.600
specific. I don't know if any of you

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:55.120
guys watch The Bachelor, but I only

00:12:53.600 --> 00:12:56.839
watched a couple of seasons a long time

00:12:55.120 --> 00:12:58.960
ago, and I remember in one of them there

00:12:56.839 --> 00:13:00.440
was a guy named Joe. Just Joe who was on

00:12:58.960 --> 00:13:02.440
the show. He could have been eliminated

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:04.440
in episode one for all I know. But then

00:13:02.440 --> 00:13:06.240
we learned that he worked at a grocery

00:13:04.440 --> 00:13:08.520
store. Instead of hiding that or being

00:13:06.240 --> 00:13:10.880
embarrassed about it, he leaned all the

00:13:08.520 --> 00:13:12.920
way in, and he was grocery store Joe.

00:13:10.880 --> 00:13:14.800
That one specific detail changed the

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:16.920
whole trajectory of his life, and he

00:13:14.800 --> 00:13:18.240
became a massively beloved contestant

00:13:16.920 --> 00:13:20.200
across The Bachelor and there are so

00:13:18.240 --> 00:13:22.320
many seasons. He even got on other

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:24.560
reality TV shows. He met his wife on

00:13:22.320 --> 00:13:26.400
another Bachelor spin-off show. None of

00:13:24.560 --> 00:13:28.560
that would happen if it's just Joe, but

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:30.000
he's grocery store Joe, and he actually

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:32.480
work at a grocery store. That is such a

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.120
specific and also authentic detail about

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:35.840
himself and he made it a thing. So,

00:13:34.120 --> 00:13:37.000
think about it. What's your thing? When

00:13:35.840 --> 00:13:38.440
you have a signature, people have

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.840
something concrete to attach their

00:13:38.440 --> 00:13:42.040
curiosity to. They also think about you

00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:43.640
and then they also think about that

00:13:42.040 --> 00:13:44.880
thing. When they see something that

00:13:43.640 --> 00:13:46.640
relates to your signature, they will

00:13:44.880 --> 00:13:48.040
also think about you. So, ultimately you

00:13:46.640 --> 00:13:49.720
have to be building something worth

00:13:48.040 --> 00:13:52.200
being curious about, whether it's the

00:13:49.720 --> 00:13:53.880
signature or even substance. You have to

00:13:52.200 --> 00:13:55.960
be reading, creating things,

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:58.320
experiencing, growing, developing new

00:13:55.960 --> 00:14:00.480
skills, nurturing your passions because

00:13:58.320 --> 00:14:02.960
mystery without substance is just

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:05.080
nothing. It's giving nothing and nobody

00:14:02.960 --> 00:14:06.640
is fascinated by nothing. The question

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:08.480
isn't about how do I seem more

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:10.920
interesting, but really am I investing

00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:12.360
in myself enough to become someone worth

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:13.920
writing home about. So, if you look at

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:15.560
your own life and you realize there's

00:14:13.920 --> 00:14:17.600
nothing interesting about you, you have

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:20.080
to go and create something for yourself.

00:14:17.600 --> 00:14:22.480
Strategic silence is the power of the

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:24.480
unsaid. Robert Greene wrote in The 48

00:14:22.480 --> 00:14:26.560
Laws of Power that everything is judged

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:28.440
by its appearance and what is unseen

00:14:26.560 --> 00:14:30.000
counts for nothing. And while I think

00:14:28.440 --> 00:14:32.120
Greene may be right about the power of

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.440
perception because people judge me by my

00:14:32.120 --> 00:14:36.839
appearance all the time, I also think

00:14:34.440 --> 00:14:39.320
the opposite is true. Sometimes what is

00:14:36.839 --> 00:14:41.640
unseen also counts for everything and

00:14:39.320 --> 00:14:43.240
that is the art of communication. The

00:14:41.640 --> 00:14:44.720
words you don't say carry more weight

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:46.520
than the words you do. [music] Think

00:14:44.720 --> 00:14:47.920
about a person who speak calmly at a

00:14:46.520 --> 00:14:50.080
meeting and they're the last ones to

00:14:47.920 --> 00:14:51.680
talk. Everyone else has had a turn

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:53.400
talking over one another trying to prove

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:55.720
themselves and then this one person who

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:58.040
has just been observing everything steps

00:14:55.720 --> 00:15:00.360
in and says something precise and

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:02.000
everyone's like, "Whoa." You will feel

00:15:00.360 --> 00:15:03.600
the energy in the room all shifting

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:05.360
towards this one person because they

00:15:03.600 --> 00:15:06.680
talk last and they talk later. Every

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:08.920
word that they say actually is

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:10.680
remembered with even more impact and I

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:12.120
have learned that the hard way. I used

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:13.720
to think that if I had a thought, it

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:15.560
needed to come out and I had to say it.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:17.240
I also blame Twitter culture for this

00:15:15.560 --> 00:15:19.040
because you remember back in 2012 when

00:15:17.240 --> 00:15:20.800
everyone was just being manic and spam

00:15:19.040 --> 00:15:22.840
tweeting their streams of consciousness

00:15:20.800 --> 00:15:25.080
and then 5 years later, all of those

00:15:22.840 --> 00:15:27.240
tweets came back to haunt them. Yeah,

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:29.720
exactly. By saying everything, we're

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:31.480
actually diluting the power of anything.

00:15:29.720 --> 00:15:33.800
Not to mention, any kind of information

00:15:31.480 --> 00:15:35.680
that we share about us can be weaponized

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:37.440
against us. So, if they don't know, they

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:39.320
can't use it against you. How do we

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:41.320
practice this? Before you speak, ask

00:15:39.320 --> 00:15:43.480
yourself, "Does this need to be said?

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:45.200
Does this need to be said by me? And if

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:47.240
it needs to be said by me right now?"

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:49.480
And if the answer to any of those is no,

00:15:47.240 --> 00:15:50.880
then let the silence speak for itself.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:53.360
Sometimes people instinctually

00:15:50.880 --> 00:15:55.200
overcorrect by becoming the class clown,

00:15:53.360 --> 00:15:56.920
for example, and they start deflecting

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.640
with humor, and their vulnerability

00:15:56.920 --> 00:16:00.240
becomes a joke. But, that's also you

00:15:58.640 --> 00:16:02.480
building a wall as well. Don't get me

00:16:00.240 --> 00:16:04.200
wrong, being funny is such a gift, but

00:16:02.480 --> 00:16:06.040
if that's how you're actually practicing

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:07.600
avoidance, then you're just hiding

00:16:06.040 --> 00:16:10.360
behind that instead of genuinely

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:12.800
expressing who you truly are. The point

00:16:10.360 --> 00:16:14.680
of cultivating mystique is not to build

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:16.680
up even more walls around you, but to

00:16:14.680 --> 00:16:18.520
need less of it. So, if you're thinking,

00:16:16.680 --> 00:16:20.320
"But, May, I'm a talker. I love to

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:22.440
express myself, and that's just who I

00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:23.960
am." I totally hear you. We're not being

00:16:22.440 --> 00:16:25.560
someone that we're not. We're being more

00:16:23.960 --> 00:16:27.839
intentional. We can still be warm and

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:29.360
vibrant and expressive, and choose to

00:16:27.839 --> 00:16:31.280
reveal information about yourself when

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:32.600
it suits the situation. So, it's not

00:16:31.280 --> 00:16:35.120
really about speaking less, but really

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:37.720
reveal less, right? You can still be the

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:38.880
life of the party, and be fun, without

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:40.440
anyone actually knowing what you're

00:16:38.880 --> 00:16:41.760
going through. And trust me, I have been

00:16:40.440 --> 00:16:43.440
through plenty of things where I don't

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:45.600
say a word, and only when I'm able to

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.800
figure things out for myself, and think,

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:50.480
"Okay, there actually lessons I can pass

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:52.240
on here." Only then do I speak about

00:16:50.480 --> 00:16:54.040
negative things. That's the power of

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:55.800
being intentional is that it's only us

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:57.960
saying enough to make people desperate

00:16:55.800 --> 00:17:00.200
to learn more about us. Unshakeable

00:16:57.960 --> 00:17:01.960
calmness, being a true stoic is the

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:04.319
rarest form of power, and it is

00:17:01.960 --> 00:17:06.240
incredibly, amazingly powerful. Because,

00:17:04.319 --> 00:17:08.240
have you been around someone who just

00:17:06.240 --> 00:17:10.520
doesn't react to anything? They're very

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:12.400
grounded, like, "I'm okay, regardless of

00:17:10.520 --> 00:17:14.480
what happens, even if everyone around me

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:15.959
is on fire." They don't crumble, they

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:18.160
don't crash out, and they're able to

00:17:15.959 --> 00:17:20.199
make everyone feel more calm just by

00:17:18.160 --> 00:17:22.120
being around them. That is so super

00:17:20.199 --> 00:17:23.640
absolutely magnetic and it's very rare,

00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:26.160
which makes it even more valuable

00:17:23.640 --> 00:17:28.280
because most people I realize are so

00:17:26.160 --> 00:17:30.200
emotionally reactive. They're on a

00:17:28.280 --> 00:17:32.160
constant roller coaster and it makes

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:33.800
them super easy to manipulate, too, by

00:17:32.160 --> 00:17:35.520
the way, to be honest with you. If you

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:37.360
meet someone who's regulated, on the

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:38.920
other hand, and their internal state

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:41.800
doesn't quite depend on external

00:17:38.920 --> 00:17:43.560
circumstances, it's almost unsettling in

00:17:41.800 --> 00:17:45.280
the best way. And that's low-key what

00:17:43.560 --> 00:17:46.720
everybody wants, but you can't quite

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:48.440
name what it is because you don't know

00:17:46.720 --> 00:17:50.680
what it truly is. And what it is

00:17:48.440 --> 00:17:51.960
actually is sovereignty. They fully

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:53.960
belong to themselves. They're not

00:17:51.960 --> 00:17:55.800
letting everyone else affect them. Their

00:17:53.960 --> 00:17:57.440
mood doesn't belong to the weather or to

00:17:55.800 --> 00:17:59.760
opinions or being triggered by the

00:17:57.440 --> 00:18:02.440
algorithm or giving into rage bait. A

00:17:59.760 --> 00:18:04.960
stable internal mind is also the

00:18:02.440 --> 00:18:07.200
foundation of being mysterious, which

00:18:04.960 --> 00:18:09.200
also makes them unpredictable as well

00:18:07.200 --> 00:18:11.360
and very intriguing. And you're like,

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:13.000
"What do they know that I don't?" Here's

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:14.360
a very simple version of this I can give

00:18:13.000 --> 00:18:16.400
you. Basically, just show up, have a

00:18:14.360 --> 00:18:18.000
good time, and be present, and act like

00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:19.400
you're not keeping score of anything.

00:18:18.000 --> 00:18:20.760
And don't lose yourself when things

00:18:19.400 --> 00:18:23.280
don't go the way that you want. And

00:18:20.760 --> 00:18:25.400
that's pretty much it. Stay calm, be

00:18:23.280 --> 00:18:27.400
confident, and being precise, that is so

00:18:25.400 --> 00:18:29.680
magnetic because it shows you know what

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:31.800
being safe feels like and you are a safe

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:33.040
person. People are able to relax around

00:18:31.800 --> 00:18:34.840
you. They don't have to feel like

00:18:33.040 --> 00:18:36.680
they're managing your emotions or walk

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:38.320
on eggshells around you or have to

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:40.440
figure out which version of you is going

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:41.960
to show up today. That consistency is so

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:43.760
rare that people are drawn to that. I

00:18:41.960 --> 00:18:45.240
know this because I used to be hot and

00:18:43.760 --> 00:18:46.800
cold and people would walk around me

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:48.920
like they're walking on eggshells and

00:18:46.800 --> 00:18:50.360
ultimately it literally ruined my life

00:18:48.920 --> 00:18:52.200
because people could not wait to get rid

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:53.960
of me. When I make these videos and I

00:18:52.200 --> 00:18:55.480
say these things to you, I truly don't

00:18:53.960 --> 00:18:57.160
want anyone else to go down that path.

00:18:55.480 --> 00:18:58.760
And it's not about being fake, either.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:00.840
We're not putting up a front here. This

00:18:58.760 --> 00:19:02.960
is basically a byproduct of inner

00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:04.480
security. When you contain your

00:19:02.960 --> 00:19:06.360
insecurities, don't get me wrong.

00:19:04.480 --> 00:19:08.480
Everyone is insecure about something. It

00:19:06.360 --> 00:19:10.960
doesn't matter who you are. But despite

00:19:08.480 --> 00:19:12.840
our insecurities, you can still be

00:19:10.960 --> 00:19:14.560
genuinely at home with yourself and

00:19:12.840 --> 00:19:16.800
you're also comfortable with yourself

00:19:14.560 --> 00:19:19.160
regardless and you don't seek validation

00:19:16.800 --> 00:19:20.680
through oversharing, then you won't need

00:19:19.160 --> 00:19:22.400
other people's reactions to feel a

00:19:20.680 --> 00:19:24.280
certain way about yourself. A lot of

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:25.440
people misunderstand when I say be more

00:19:24.280 --> 00:19:27.520
mysterious and they think that it's

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:29.240
something toxic. So here are a few

00:19:27.520 --> 00:19:30.840
prerequisites because if you don't have

